Venetium 0021 - GPU on Windows ARM32: ANGLE's D3D9 backend (feature level 9_x hardware such as the Surface 2's Tegra).

BATCH-ARM-1 section 3E, his decision 9 (ARM-1-DECISIONS.md). CR77's GPU solution (SUPERMIUM-3 section 2, GPU-PORT-LIST-150.md),
re-derived for 150. 3 files:
- third_party/angle/gni/angle.gni: angle_enable_d3d11 and angle_enable_vulkan are off for current_cpu == "arm"; D3D9 and GL stay on.
  (gn args on out/arm-rt21: angle_enable_d3d11 = false, angle_enable_d3d9 = true, angle_enable_vulkan = false, angle_enable_gl = true.)
- ui/gl/gl_features.cc: kAllowANGLED3D9Fallback is enabled by default on Windows ARM32 only (x86/x64/arm64 keep DISABLED): without it
  ARM32 would get neither D3D11 (excluded) nor D3D9 (gated off) - no ANGLE display at all.
- third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/d3d9/Renderer9.cpp: ANGLE_SUPPORT_SHADER_MODEL_2 = 1 for _M_ARM only (pixel shader 2.0,
  feature level 9_x); other targets keep shader model 3.
CR77's NPOT hunk is dropped (his decision: a no-op on Windows 10). SwiftShader and ANGLE's WebGPU backend are off for ARM in
venetium/args/out-arm-rt21.gn (args, not this patch).
Checked (RUNTIME, real arm-rt21 graph after gn gen): 399 ANGLE objects including the D3D9 backend and gl_features.obj compile as
ARMNT; linking libGLESv2/libEGL waits on libc++ (TOOLCHAIN-ISSUES, ARM32 C++ EH). Device-only: D3D9 on the Tegra at FL 9_x.

